# shadcn/ui — The Only UI Allowed in This Project

This project uses shadcn with [components.json](mdc:components.json). UI primitives live under `src/components/ui/` (alias `@/components/ui`).

## Absolute Rule: No Custom UI

**NEVER create custom UI components, custom CSS classes for layout/styling, or hand-rolled UI primitives.** Every piece of UI must come from the shadcn/ui registry. This includes — but is not limited to — buttons, inputs, dialogs, cards, dropdowns, badges, toasts, and navigation elements.

**This project is in dark mode, so make sure sure there are no dark colored text on dark backgrounds (and vice versa)**

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — custom button
<button className="bg-blue-500 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded">Click me</button>

// ❌ BAD — hand-rolled card
<div className="border rounded-lg p-4 shadow">...</div>

// ✅ GOOD — shadcn/ui components only
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { Card, CardContent } from "@/components/ui/card";
<Button>Click me</Button>
<Card><CardContent>...</CardContent></Card>
```

## Clerk Auth UI: shadcn Button + Modal Mode

Clerk sign-in and sign-up must **never** render inline flows or redirect to a hosted Clerk page. All auth must be triggered by a shadcn `Button` that opens Clerk in **modal** mode.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — Clerk's own button component
import { SignInButton } from "@clerk/nextjs";
<SignInButton />

// ❌ BAD — redirect mode
<SignInButton mode="redirect" />

// ✅ GOOD — shadcn Button wrapping Clerk in modal mode
import { SignInButton, SignUpButton } from "@clerk/nextjs";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";

<SignInButton mode="modal">
  <Button>Sign in</Button>
</SignInButton>

<SignUpButton mode="modal">
  <Button>Sign up</Button>
</SignUpButton>
```

## When to install

Whenever you add or rely on an import from `@/components/ui/<name>` (or equivalent path to `src/components/ui/<name>.tsx`), **check that the file exists**. If it is missing, **install the component** — do not leave the app with unresolved imports or ask the user to run the CLI manually unless the command cannot run (for example, network blocked).

## Command

From the repository root:

```bash
npx shadcn add <component> -y
```

- Use the **registry component name** (kebab-case), e.g. `dialog`, `dropdown-menu`, `card`.
- For several missing pieces in one pass: `npx shadcn add dialog dropdown-menu -y`
- `-y` skips confirmation (non-interactive).

Registry and behavior are defined by [components.json](mdc:components.json); do not hand-copy component source from the docs unless `shadcn add` fails and you must document the error.

## After install

Confirm the new file(s) under `src/components/ui/`, fix any import paths to match project aliases, and run lint/typecheck if you touched types or exports.
